      "role": "user",
      "content": "{\"role\": \"B\", \"goal\": \"legal SIMD/vectorization and loop dependencies\", \"experiment\": \"cc9f19192caa46fa-h01\", \"ordinal\": 2, \"integration_source_ids\": [], \"current_source_paths\": [\"src/model-view/primetest.c\", \"src/sources/primetest.c\"], \"context_as_data\": {\"sources\": [], \"interactions\": [], \"automatic_observations\": {\"baseline\": {\"experiment_id\": \"baseline-e1\", \"outcome\": {\"status\": \"valid\", \"correct\": true, \"score\": 0.5, \"mean_seconds\": 0.043314365980525814}, \"raw_logs\": [{\"status\": \"failed\", \"code\": \"unavailable_diagnostic\"}, {\"status\": \"completed\", \"code\": \"check_passed\"}]}, \"selected_parent\": {\"experiment_id\": \"858b41bbfa154b01\", \"role\": \"B\", \"hypothesis\": \"Four independent exact divisibility tests per AArch64 NEON vector should accelerate primality testing by replacing repeated floating-point fmod calls with unsigned multiplication and comparison.\", \"outcome\": {\"status\": \"valid\", \"correct\": true, \"score\": 0.8991578302968596, \"mean_seconds\": 0.004857784137129784}, \"raw_logs\": [{\"status\": \"failed\", \"code\": \"unavailable_diagnostic\"}, {\"status\": \"completed\", \"code\": \"check_passed\"}]}, \"selected_base_commit\": \"fb159e261d78d3b8f4eb24c62bddf3d19f90e0e9\", \"recent_own_role\": [{\"experiment_id\": \"858b41bbfa154b01\", \"role\": \"B\", \"hypothesis\": \"Four independent exact divisibility tests per AArch64 NEON vector should accelerate primality testing by replacing repeated floating-point fmod calls with unsigned multiplication and comparison.\", \"outcome\": {\"status\": \"valid\", \"correct\": true, \"score\": 0.8991578302968596, \"mean_seconds\": 0.004857784137129784}, \"raw_logs\": [{\"status\": \"failed\", \"code\": \"unavailable_diagnostic\"}, {\"status\": \"completed\", \"code\": \"check_passed\"}]}], \"own_role_history\": [{\"experiment_id\": \"858b41bbfa154b01\", \"status\": \"valid\", \"correct\": true, \"score\": 0.8991578302968596, \"mean_seconds\": 0.004857784137129784}], \"node_development\": {\"attempt\": 1, \"remaining_attempts\": 3, \"previous_attempts\": [], \"confirmation_data_available\": false}}, \"documents_as_data\": [], \"deadline\": 1792286362.2930386, \"generation_deadline\": 1792286362.2930386, \"protocol_id\": \"736652daff2c790cceeb5ac90a060a9a4bd0af109e2da7f85a782a3b0b277c5a\", \"remaining_tokens\": 589824, \"official_statement_as_data\": \"Problem E\\nYet More Primes\\nPrime test is a common task in many applications, specially for security, cryptography,\\nand other interest areas. There are a number of techniques used to verify if a number is\\nprime, and the common problem is that all techniques consumes lots of time.\\nThe problem is easy to solve, giving the number to be tested and time enough to calculate.\\nBut a weird scientist took our numbers, and cut them in two halves, so we have ﬁrst to\\nre-arrange the numbers, looking for the primes. In this case, we have the certainty that all\\nthe numbers we have are primes, but the problem is how to re-order them\\nInput\\nIn the ﬁrst line, there is the numberP of prime numbers (1≤ P≤ 1000). Then, 2P lines\\nwith parts of the numbers to be tested, with no order. Prime numbers in this problem are\\ntaken as strings, so ﬁrst half and second half simply means an arbitrary cut of such string.\\nFor instance, prime number 504155039 can be cut in 5041 and 55039, or 504155 and 039\\nNote that second half numbers could begin with a lead zero, so you must take it into\\naccount. Of course, this doesn’t happen with the ﬁrst half.\\nThe input must be read from the standard input.\\nOutput\\nYou have to print the list of the P prime numbers, in ascendant order.\\nThe output must be written to the standard output.\\nExample\\nInput Output\\n4 1000213\\n50415 5041501\\n100 5575001\\n5041 504155039\\n55750 504155713\\n5039\\n01\\n0213\\n55713\\n\\n\\nThis experiment uses a reviewed finite certified input/output contract only. There are six private research cases and six distinct private confirmation cases. P is in {1,2,4,8,16,30}; the input lists two separately permuted groups of P decimal fragments. Left fragments have no leading zero and end in an even digit; right fragments have seven characters including a leading zero. Each original pair comes from a true prime and the multiset of every admissible prime concatenation equals the P source occurrences. Concatenations are at most 600971707; output is compared as exact bytes. The official example has an unresolved P/output-count contradiction. No claim is made for the whole contest domain or arbitrary fragment orders. The fixed benchmark is one member of the same certified finite set; no hidden values or expected outputs are supplied. Target: Linux ARM64, four CPU cores, 16 GiB RAM, zero GPUs. Compilation: GCC -O2 -std=c11 -Werror=uninitialized -Werror=maybe-uninitialized -lm.\", \"runtime_as_data\": {\"cpu_cores\": 4, \"OMP_NUM_THREADS\": 4, \"architecture\": \"ARM64\", \"candidate_GPU\": false, \"comparison\": \"Exact output bytes against official reference\"}, \"mother_model_as_data\": {\"phase\": \"preparation\", \"status\": \"complete\", \"guidance\": \"Research contract-derived matching and batch pruning. First establish the invariant: the source pairs provide a perfect matching, and exactly P prime edges means every fragment occurrence has exactly one prime partner. Represent surviving columns with bitmasks; reject proven composites using small-prime residue filters, sharing left-offset and suffix residues across candidates. Propagate forced row/column singletons; otherwise use exact primality tests to identify an edge before removing its endpoints. Never assume the input permutations align. Tune the filtering cutoff and measure whether reduced primality work repays bookkeeping overhead. This matching shortcut is valid only under the certified contract, not the unrestricted contest statement.\", \"analysis\": \"The only measured implementation is the correct baseline: mean 0.043314365980525814 seconds. There are no measured optimization results or hotspot diagnostics. Floating-point trial division and repeated string conversion are plausible bottlenecks, not established profiles. The certified contract limits work to 900 concatenations, values at most 600971707, and trial divisors at most 24514. Numeric concatenation is left*10^7+right; leading zeros must still determine suffix width. Small workloads favor serial implementations and careful accounting for startup costs. Use the certified contract rather than resolving the contradictory example or assuming broader contest coverage; all valid certified inputs must remain correct.\", \"origin\": \"model output from this fresh run; no operator analysis\"}}, \"required_json_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"hypothesis\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"transformations\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"sources_kept\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"uniqueItems\": true, \"maxItems\": 0}, \"files\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"path\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"content\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"path\", \"content\"]}}, \"notes\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"hypothesis\", \"transformations\", \"sources_kept\", \"files\", \"notes\"]}}\n\nCURRENT SOURCE AS DATA:\n\n--- BEGIN FILE src/model-view/primetest.c ---\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\n#if defined(__aarch64__) && defined(__ARM_NEON)\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n#endif\n\n#define MAXNUM 100\n#define MAXSTR 50\n#define MAXRESULTS 1000\n#define MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR 65535u\n#define TRIAL_CAPACITY ((MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR + 1u) / 2u)\n\nchar firstHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\nchar secondHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\nchar strToTest[MAXSTR];\nlong int result[MAXRESULTS];\nint numPrimes=0;\n\nstatic uint32_t trial_square[TRIAL_CAPACITY];\nstatic uint32_t trial_inverse[TRIAL_CAPACITY];\nstatic uint32_t trial_threshold[TRIAL_CAPACITY];\nstatic unsigned int trial_count=0;\nstatic int trial_ready=0;\n\nstatic void initialize_trial_divisors(void)\n{\n    static unsigned char composite[MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR + 1u];\n    memset(composite, 0, sizeof composite);\n    trial_count=0;\n\n    for (uint32_t p=3u; p<=MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR; p+=2u) {\n        if (composite[p])\n            continue;\n\n        uint32_t inverse=1u;\n        for (int step=0; step<5; ++step)\n            inverse *= 2u - p * inverse;\n\n        uint32_t square=p*p;\n        trial_square[trial_count]=square;\n        trial_inverse[trial_count]=inverse;\n        trial_threshold[trial_count]=UINT32_MAX/p;\n        ++trial_count;\n\n        if (square<=MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR) {\n            for (uint32_t multiple=square;\n                 multiple<=MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR; multiple+=2u*p)\n                composite[multiple]=1;\n        }\n    }\n    trial_ready=1;\n}\n\nint isprime(long int value)\n{\n    if (value<2)\n        return 0;\n    if ((value & 1L)==0)\n        return value==2;\n\n    if ((uint64_t)value>UINT32_MAX) {\n        for (long int factor=3; factor<=value/factor; factor+=2)\n            if (value%factor==0)\n                return 0;\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    uint32_t n=(uint32_t)value;\n    if (!trial_ready)\n        initialize_trial_divisors();\n\n    unsigned int i=0;\n#if defined(__aarch64__) && defined(__ARM_NEON)\n    uint32x4_t input=vdupq_n_u32(n);\n    for (; i+3u<trial_count && trial_square[i+3u]<=n; i+=4u) {\n        uint32x4_t products=vmulq_u32(\n            input, vld1q_u32(trial_inverse+i));\n        uint32x4_t divides=vcleq_u32(\n            products, vld1q_u32(trial_threshold+i));\n        if (vmaxvq_u32(divides)!=0u)\n            return 0;\n    }\n#endif\n\n    /* For odd p, n is divisible by p exactly when the wrapped\n       product n*inverse(p) is at most UINT32_MAX/p. */\n    for (; i<trial_count && trial_square[i]<=n; ++i)\n        if ((uint32_t)(n*trial_inverse[i])<=trial_threshold[i])\n            return 0;\n    return 1;\n}\n\nvoid quicksort(long int *primes,int first,int last)\n{ int i, j, pivot;\n  long int temp;\n\n  if (first<last)\n     { pivot=first;\n       i=first;\n       j=last;\n       while(i<j)\n         { while (primes[i]<=primes[pivot]&&i<last)\n             i++;\n           while(primes[j]>primes[pivot])\n             j--;\n           if (i<j)\n              { temp=primes[i];\n                primes[i]=primes[j];\n                primes[j]=temp;\n              }\n         }\n       temp=primes[pivot];\n       primes[pivot]=primes[j];\n       primes[j]=temp;\n       quicksort(primes,first,j-1);\n       quicksort(primes,j+1,last);\n     }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char** argv)\n{ FILE *primesFile;\n  int i=0,j=0,numResults=0;\n  long int primeToTest;\n  primesFile=stdin;\n  fscanf(primesFile,\"%d\\n\",&numPrimes);\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\n      fscanf(primesFile,\"%s\\n\",firstHalf[i]);\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\n      fscanf(primesFile,\"%s\\n\",secondHalf[i]);\n  fclose(primesFile);\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\n      for (j=0;j<numPrimes;j++)\n          { strcpy(strToTest,firstHalf[i]);\n            strcat(strToTest,secondHalf[j]);\n            primeToTest=atol(strToTest);\n            if (isprime(primeToTest))\n               { result[numResults++]=primeToTest;\n               }\n          }\n  quicksort(result,0,numResults-1);\n  for (i=0;i<numResults;i++)\n      printf(\"%ld\\n\",result[i]);\n  return 0;\n}\n\n--- END FILE src/model-view/primetest.c ---\n\n--- BEGIN FILE src/sources/primetest.c ---\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\n#if defined(__aarch64__) && defined(__ARM_NEON)\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n#endif\n\n#define MAXNUM 100\n#define MAXSTR 50\n#define MAXRESULTS 1000\n#define MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR 65535u\n#define TRIAL_CAPACITY ((MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR + 1u) / 2u)\n\nchar firstHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\nchar secondHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\nchar strToTest[MAXSTR];\nlong int result[MAXRESULTS];\nint numPrimes=0;\n\nstatic uint32_t trial_square[TRIAL_CAPACITY];\nstatic uint32_t trial_inverse[TRIAL_CAPACITY];\nstatic uint32_t trial_threshold[TRIAL_CAPACITY];\nstatic unsigned int trial_count=0;\nstatic int trial_ready=0;\n\nstatic void initialize_trial_divisors(void)\n{\n    static unsigned char composite[MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR + 1u];\n    memset(composite, 0, sizeof composite);\n    trial_count=0;\n\n    for (uint32_t p=3u; p<=MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR; p+=2u) {\n        if (composite[p])\n            continue;\n\n        uint32_t inverse=1u;\n        for (int step=0; step<5; ++step)\n            inverse *= 2u - p * inverse;\n\n        uint32_t square=p*p;\n        trial_square[trial_count]=square;\n        trial_inverse[trial_count]=inverse;\n        trial_threshold[trial_count]=UINT32_MAX/p;\n        ++trial_count;\n\n        if (square<=MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR) {\n            for (uint32_t multiple=square;\n                 multiple<=MAX_TRIAL_FACTOR; multiple+=2u*p)\n                composite[multiple]=1;\n        }\n    }\n    trial_ready=1;\n}\n\nint isprime(long int value)\n{\n    if (value<2)\n        return 0;\n    if ((value & 1L)==0)\n        return value==2;\n\n    if ((uint64_t)value>UINT32_MAX) {\n        for (long int factor=3; factor<=value/factor; factor+=2)\n            if (value%factor==0)\n                return 0;\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    uint32_t n=(uint32_t)value;\n    if (!trial_ready)\n        initialize_trial_divisors();\n\n    unsigned int i=0;\n#if defined(__aarch64__) && defined(__ARM_NEON)\n    uint32x4_t input=vdupq_n_u32(n);\n    for (; i+3u<trial_count && trial_square[i+3u]<=n; i+=4u) {\n        uint32x4_t products=vmulq_u32(\n            input, vld1q_u32(trial_inverse+i));\n        uint32x4_t divides=vcleq_u32(\n            products, vld1q_u32(trial_threshold+i));\n        if (vmaxvq_u32(divides)!=0u)\n            return 0;\n    }\n#endif\n\n    /* For odd p, n is divisible by p exactly when the wrapped\n       product n*inverse(p) is at most UINT32_MAX/p. */\n    for (; i<trial_count && trial_square[i]<=n; ++i)\n        if ((uint32_t)(n*trial_inverse[i])<=trial_threshold[i])\n            return 0;\n    return 1;\n}\n\nvoid quicksort(long int *primes,int first,int last)\n{ int i, j, pivot;\n  long int temp;\n\n  if (first<last)\n     { pivot=first;\n       i=first;\n       j=last;\n       while(i<j)\n         { while (primes[i]<=primes[pivot]&&i<last)\n             i++;\n           while(primes[j]>primes[pivot])\n             j--;\n           if (i<j)\n              { temp=primes[i];\n                primes[i]=primes[j];\n                primes[j]=temp;\n              }\n         }\n       temp=primes[pivot];\n       primes[pivot]=primes[j];\n       primes[j]=temp;\n       quicksort(primes,first,j-1);\n       quicksort(primes,j+1,last);\n     }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char** argv)\n{ FILE *primesFile;\n  int i=0,j=0,numResults=0;\n  long int primeToTest;\n  primesFile=stdin;\n  fscanf(primesFile,\"%d\\n\",&numPrimes);\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\n      fscanf(primesFile,\"%s\\n\",firstHalf[i]);\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\n      fscanf(primesFile,\"%s\\n\",secondHalf[i]);\n  fclose(primesFile);\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\n      for (j=0;j<numPrimes;j++)\n          { strcpy(strToTest,firstHalf[i]);\n            strcat(strToTest,secondHalf[j]);\n            primeToTest=atol(strToTest);\n            if (isprime(primeToTest))\n               { result[numResults++]=primeToTest;\n               }\n          }\n  quicksort(result,0,numResults-1);\n  for (i=0;i<numResults;i++)\n      printf(\"%ld\\n\",result[i]);\n  return 0;\n}\n\n--- END FILE src/sources/primetest.c ---\n"
    }
